# SHE Dashboard Architecture

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    GH[GitHub commits / PRs / issues / reviews / checks]
    ACT[GitHub Actions]
    LED[pr-production-ledger.yml]
    BACK[context-relationship-backfill.yml]
    CORPUS[Historical Evidence Corpus]
    RED[SHE pure reducers]
    SNAP[Versioned dashboard snapshots]
    VERCEL[Vercel interactive SHE]
    PAGES[GitHub Pages static mirror]
    HEX[Hex analysis cockpit]
    MVT[DOE / MVT]
    MB[Moneyball / 3L0]
    LEARN[Learning / Manager Evolution]

    GH --> ACT
    ACT --> LED
    ACT --> BACK
    LED --> CORPUS
    BACK --> CORPUS
    GH --> CORPUS
    CORPUS --> RED
    RED --> SNAP
    SNAP --> VERCEL
    SNAP --> PAGES
    SNAP --> HEX
    CORPUS --> MVT
    MVT --> MB
    CORPUS --> MB
    MB --> LEARN
    LEARN -. policy improvement .-> ACT

    RENDER[Render / n8n examples]
    RENDER -. reference only .-> ACT
```

## Invariants

1. Git history/corpus remains the durable evidence authority.
2. Actions collect and transform; they do not erase history.
3. SHE reducers are deterministic and network-free.
4. Dashboard projections must carry source SHA, snapshot ID, generation time, and coverage state.
5. Hex is optional analysis, never the system of record.
6. Render/n8n examples are optional visual/automation references, never a free-scope dependency.
7. Partial corpus state is first-class UI state.
